# Frontend Styling (BEM SCSS)

## Naming Convention

Block names use PascalCase matching the component name. Elements use `__`, modifiers use `--`.

## Correct

```scss
.SpecCard {
  padding: 1rem;
  background: var(--surface-primary);

  &__Title {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  &__Badge {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  &--draft {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-warning);
  }

  &--published {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-success);
  }
}
```

## Incorrect — nested elements

```scss
// WRONG: never nest elements inside elements
.SpecCard {
  &__Header {
    &__Title { font-size: 1rem; }  // BAD: &__Header &__Title
    &__Icon { width: 16px; }       // BAD: &__Header &__Icon
  }
}
```

Flatten nested elements: use `&__HeaderTitle` or restructure the component.

## Rules

- Single-level nesting only. Never `&__Item` inside another `&__Item`.
- Use CSS custom properties (`var(--*)`) for theming and dark mode.
- SCSS variables (`$var`) for compile-time values only (breakpoints, z-indices).
- No `!important` unless overriding third-party CSS (add a comment explaining why).
- Co-locate styles: `ComponentName.module.scss` next to `ComponentName.tsx`.
- Global variables and mixins live in `client/ui/src/styles/`.
